  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1130 PM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nUnprecedented prolonged heat for the month of October is coming\nto an end as cooler air has pushed its way through the CWA over\nthe day's course. FROPA finally occurred at Falls City and \nNebraska's remaining square mile around 10pm. \n\nWe watched as convection developed in north-central Kansas this\nevening along that same front. Have maintained 25% PoPs along \nthe front overnight for this CWA, too, due to increased \nisentropic lift as the LLJ develops. Both EAX (KC) and OAX \n(Omaha) show increasing wind speeds over the past two hours.\nIsolated showers have developed in the Omaha metro. Expect to \nbe dry by morning.",
